.docname {Rendering}
.include {docs}

Everything document-generation related lives on `karbone.renders`, an implementation of the `Renders` interface.

## Template sources

A `TemplateSource` says where the template comes from:

```kotlin
TemplateSource.bytes(docxBytes, fileName = "invoice.docx")   // in-memory content
TemplateSource.file(Path.of("invoice.docx"))                 // local file, read lazily and cached
TemplateSource.stream("invoice.docx") { openInputStream() }  // opened and read lazily, cached
TemplateSource.id("5f3759df...")                             // a template Carbone already knows
```

The first three are `TemplateSource.Content`: their bytes are available locally, and `sha256()` gives the SHA-256 of that
content, which is also the legacy Carbone template id. `TemplateSource.id(...)` (aliased `TemplateSource.Remote`) instead
references a template already stored on Carbone, by legacy id, versioned template id, or version id — Carbone accepts all
three in the same path segment.

### Hash-first flow

Rendering from a `Content` source never requires uploading it up front:

1. Karbone computes the SHA-256 of the content and calls `POST /render/{sha256}` directly.
2. If Carbone already has a template with that hash (because it was uploaded before, by Karbone or anyone else), the render
   succeeds in one round-trip.
3. If Carbone answers 404, Karbone uploads the content with `templates.upload(...)` and retries the render exactly once.

This only applies to legacy (non-versioned) template ids: a `TemplateSource.Remote` id is used as-is and a 404 on it is raised
as `KarboneError.TemplateNotFound`, never retried.

## Render data

`RenderData` is the `data` field of the request:

```kotlin
RenderData.raw("""{"number":"F-1"}""")            // pre-serialized JSON, e.g. from Jackson or Gson
RenderData.of(jsonElement)                        // a kotlinx.serialization JsonElement
RenderData.of(myDataClass)                        // any @Serializable value, encoded by Karbone
RenderData.Empty                                  // {} — tags resolve to empty
```

`RenderData.Raw` is meant for callers who already produce JSON with another library; Karbone sends it through unmodified.
`RenderData.of(value)` requires `value`'s type to be `@Serializable` and uses Karbone's configured `Json` (see
[Configuration](configuration.qd)) to encode it.

## Render options

`RenderOptions` covers every field Carbone accepts alongside `data` and the template, built either directly or through the
DSL builder:

```kotlin
val options = RenderOptions.build {
  pdf {
    version = PdfVersion.PDF_A_3
    encryptFile = true
    documentOpenPassword = "secret"
    watermark("DRAFT") { opacity = 0.3; rotation = 45.0 }
  }
  lang = "fr-fr"
  timezone = "Europe/Paris"
  reportName = "invoice-{d.number}"
  hardRefresh = true
  header("carbone-egress-header-authorization", "Bearer downstream-token")
}
```

Each field maps 1:1 to a Carbone request field. The tables below give the shape of each group; the exhaustive list with types and
defaults is in the [API reference](@/api/index.html) (`RenderOptions`, `PdfOptions`, `ImageOptions`, `CsvOptions`).

### Output format (`convertTo`)

| Format                        | Options type   | Builder shortcut       |
| ----------------------------- | -------------- | ---------------------- |
| `OutputFormat.Pdf`            | `PdfOptions`   | `pdf { ... }`          |
| `OutputFormat.Jpg` / `Png`    | `ImageOptions` | `jpg(...)` / `png(...)` |
| `OutputFormat.Csv`            | `CsvOptions`   | `csv(...)`             |
| `OutputFormat.DOCX`, `XLSX`, `PPTX`, `ODT`, `ODS`, `ODP`, `HTML`, `TXT`, `MD`, `EPUB`, `SVG`, `WEBP` | none (`OutputFormat.Simple`) | `convertTo = OutputFormat.DOCX` |

`converter` picks the PDF engine (`LIBRE_OFFICE`, `ONLY_OFFICE`, `CHROMIUM`) and is only accepted together with a PDF output.

### PDF options, by intent

| You want to...                       | Use                                                                                       |
| ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Produce an archival PDF              | `version = PdfVersion.PDF_A_1 / PDF_A_2 / PDF_A_3`; `pdfUaCompliance`, `useTaggedPdf` for accessibility |
| Protect the document                 | `encryptFile`, `documentOpenPassword`, `permissionPassword`, `restrictPermissions`, `printing`, `changes` |
| Stamp it                             | `watermark("text") { anchor; rotation; opacity; color; size; font; fromPage; toPage }`, up to `PdfOptions.MAX_WATERMARKS`; text may use `{#PAGE_NUMBER}` and `{#PAGE_TOTAL}` |
| Control size and pages               | `pageRange` (e.g. `"1-3"`), `useLosslessCompression`, `reduceImageResolution`, `maxImageResolution` |
| Keep form fields or notes            | `exportFormFields`, `exportNotes`                                                         |

### Image and CSV options

| Type           | Fields                                                                                          |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ImageOptions` | `pixelWidth`, `pixelHeight`, `colorMode`; JPG only: `quality` (1..100); PNG only: `compression` (0..9), `interlaced`, `translucent` |
| `CsvOptions`   | `fieldSeparator`, `textDelimiter`, `characterSet` (LibreOffice charset code, `"76"` = UTF-8)     |

### Localisation and data helpers

| Field                    | Effect                                                                                     |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `timezone`               | IANA zone for `:formatD`; server default `Europe/Paris`                                    |
| `lang`                   | Locale such as `"fr-fr"`, drives `{t()}`, `:formatN`, `:formatC`                             |
| `translations`           | Dictionaries keyed by locale, used with `{t()}` and `lang`                                 |
| `enum`                   | Enumerations for the `convEnum` formatter                                                  |
| `currency`               | `CurrencyConversion(source, target, rates)` for `:formatC`                                 |
| `complement`             | Extra data reachable through `{c.}` tags                                                   |
| `variableStr`            | Predefined aliases                                                                         |

### Output and transport

| Field          | Effect                                                                                                    |
| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `reportName`   | File name returned in `Content-Disposition`; may contain Carbone tags (`"invoice-{d.number}"`)             |
| `hardRefresh`  | Recompute pagination and table of contents after rendering; requires `convertTo`                          |
| `batch`        | `BatchOptions(splitBy, output, reportName)`: one report per array item; requires `startAsync` with a webhook, rejected as `InvalidRequest` on `render` / `start` |
| `headers`      | Extra HTTP headers, e.g. `carbone-egress-header-authorization` to relay a token downstream                 |

## Sync vs. async

```kotlin
// one round trip, bytes come back directly
val doc = karbone.renders.render(template, data, options)

// two-step: get a RenderId, fetch the file later (no auth needed on download)
val id = karbone.renders.start(template, data, options)
val doc = karbone.renders.download(id)

// asynchronous: Carbone calls the webhook with {success, data: {renderId}} when done
karbone.renders.startAsync(template, data, Webhook("https://example.com/callback"), options)
```

`render` calls `POST /render/{id}?download=true` and returns the file directly. `start` calls the same endpoint with
`download=false` and returns a `RenderId` to pass to `download` (`GET /render/{renderId}`, unauthenticated; on the cloud the
file is kept for one hour and served once). `startAsync` is required for `batch` rendering and returns an
`AsyncRenderAccepted` carrying Carbone's acknowledgement message.

## Pure conversion

`convert` calls `POST /render/template`: no templating happens, tags in the document are left untouched, only the output
format changes.

```kotlin
val pdf = karbone.renders.convert(TemplateSource.bytes(docxBytes), OutputFormat.PDF)
```

Per the v5 API, omitting `data` for a conversion skips templating entirely. Some servers still behave like v4 and answer
`422` (`"Missing data"`) when `data` is absent; Karbone detects that and retries once with `data: {}`, which is equivalent for
a document with no Carbone tags. This is transparent to callers.
